.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.pytest_cache/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
output/

audit_out/
w0_out/
coupon_out/

# Normalised copies of third-party and brand source art. The upstream files are
# MFB and Reckless Systems property; this repo is public, so the derived copies
# stay local. Regenerate with tools/prep_assets.py.
assets/
!assets/normalised/bitcoin_emission_formula.svg

# Generated footprint libraries. Every footprint build_library.py installs is
# DERIVED FROM a source image, this repo is public and heading for GPLv3 /
# CERN-OHL-S, and library/ is the natural in-repo target -- so everything
# under it is ignored by default. build_library.py refuses -o inside a working
# tree that does not ignore it, and these lines are what makes the documented
# in-repo target legal for it.
#
# The two exceptions are the hand-made footprints this repo really does track:
# art_hex_asic_window (tools/texture_board.py) and art_btc_whitepaper_b
# (tools/microtext.py). Neither is reproducible by build_library.py. To track
# a further one deliberately, add another '!' line for it by name -- a blanket
# re-include of *.kicad_mod would start committing generated art.
library/*
!library/RecklessArt.pretty/
library/RecklessArt.pretty/*
!library/RecklessArt.pretty/art_hex_asic_window.kicad_mod
!library/RecklessArt.pretty/art_btc_whitepaper_b.kicad_mod

# Colour renders of source artwork. build_library.py no longer writes any --
# round 4 removed the feature outright -- but `emit_art.py --preview` still
# does, on demand, and a preview is a clean recognisable render of the SOURCE
# art: a verifier opened AdvLib.pretty.previews/satoshi_points_20mm.png and
# identified the MFB character from it. Consent to place the mark on a board
# is not permission to redistribute the art.
*.previews/

# build_library.py needs NO RULE HERE. It creates no working directory in this
# tree at all: every piece is emitted to a unique temporary file in the SYSTEM
# temporary directory, verified there, and installed with one os.replace. The
# only thing it ever writes into the library besides footprints is a
# cross-device install temporary that is unlinked in the same call.
#
# Rounds 2-4 each moved a NAMED, PERSISTENT staging directory somewhere new,
# and each new home came with its own destruction path. A dot-prefixed
# working-directory rule lived here, and in SatoshiStarter, only because the
# tool insisted on leaving directories in somebody's repo. Round 5 removed
# the subsystem instead, and the rule went with it.
